WEBVTT

00:02:10.490 --> 00:02:11.940
Stop at the corner, please.

00:02:38.540 --> 00:02:39.640
Mr. Froney.

00:02:39.640 --> 00:02:40.780
Yes, Monsieur.

00:02:40.780 --> 00:02:41.780
Can I speak to you for a moment?

00:02:41.780 --> 00:02:49.590
Well, I've been studying painting with you for some time now.

00:02:49.590 --> 00:02:52.070
Do you think it's worth my while to go on?

00:02:52.070 --> 00:02:53.070
Why do you ask?

00:02:53.070 --> 00:02:56.060
Well, I feel there's no sense in my staying here unless I have talent.

00:02:56.060 --> 00:03:00.000
If you are not certain about your talent, why did you stay on tour?

00:03:00.000 --> 00:03:06.730
now because all this is so so beautiful to me in my youth it was all so beautiful to me

00:03:06.730 --> 00:03:15.280
but now it is the city of lost illusions is your studio very far no not very let us go there you

00:03:15.280 --> 00:03:30.000
will show me what you have done yes have you any money a little not enough to live on

00:03:37.070 --> 00:03:40.560
- Then I must tell you, there is no talent here,

00:03:40.560 --> 00:03:43.400
merely industry and intelligence.

00:03:43.400 --> 00:03:45.890
You will never be anything but mediocre.

00:03:45.890 --> 00:03:49.210
And it is very cruel to discover one's mediocrity

00:03:49.210 --> 00:03:52.050
only when it is too late.

00:03:52.050 --> 00:03:55.240
- I know.

00:03:55.240 --> 00:03:56.460
Do you see that?

00:03:56.460 --> 00:03:58.540
That name does not belong there.

00:03:58.540 --> 00:03:59.860
It belongs somewhere else.

00:04:00.990 --> 00:04:04.160
Take your courage in both your hands and make something of your life.

00:04:04.160 --> 00:04:16.010
Have you anything in mind?

00:04:16.010 --> 00:04:21.850
Well, you see, I have my limitations.

00:04:21.850 --> 00:04:25.010
My father was a doctor. I've always been interested in medicine.

00:04:25.010 --> 00:04:29.250
And if one can't be great, at least one can be of some use to people.

00:05:17.850 --> 00:05:22.630
should have such a thing upon my word, I don't. I've never had a day's illness in my life. You've

00:05:22.630 --> 00:05:26.890
only got to look at me to know that. It's what we call a winter cough. A great many

00:05:26.890 --> 00:05:30.000
middle-aged women have it. Never, that's a lie.

00:05:30.030 --> 00:05:34.630
thing to say to a lady. No one's ever called me middle-aged before. Oh, it's time you got

00:05:34.630 --> 00:05:39.470
used to it. All the same, you're a nice one, dearie. Unfortunately, I can't say the same

00:05:39.470 --> 00:05:45.030
for you. Good day, madam. That'll be all now. The rest you come back tomorrow. Get him

00:05:45.030 --> 00:06:00.000
ready. All right, sir. You the boy's father? Yes, sir. What's the matter with you now? You see what

00:06:00.090 --> 00:06:06.260
enough what the matter is. The boy has a club foot. Oh, uh, Carrie, you better take this case.

00:06:06.540 --> 00:06:19.660
It's a subject you ought to know something about. It's only for the looks of the thing, you know.

00:06:19.840 --> 00:06:25.930
I don't find it no trouble. Don't you? That's wonderful. I always did. Oh, that's because you

00:06:25.930 --> 00:06:30.000
let them go on at you. You seem to be a little slow, Carrie. I think I'll have to instruct you.

00:06:30.000 --> 00:06:36.250
class. There are many varieties of club feet. This is one of the less interesting. Yours

00:06:36.250 --> 00:06:39.720
would probably prove more interesting. You have telepizaquinus, haven't you?

00:06:40.760 --> 00:06:41.870
Yes, I believe so.

00:06:42.050 --> 00:06:43.430
Don't mind taking off a sock, do you, Kerry?

00:06:48.270 --> 00:06:49.750
No, not at all.

00:07:05.950 --> 00:07:07.950
Keeps his feet nice and clean, doesn't he?

00:07:07.950 --> 00:07:12.140
Hmm, yes. Just as I thought.

00:07:12.140 --> 00:07:14.680
Telepes Aquinas.

00:07:14.680 --> 00:07:16.680
Malformation requiring you to walk on the outside of the foot.

00:07:16.680 --> 00:07:19.680
A very interesting example, I must say.

00:07:19.680 --> 00:07:21.470
Do you mind if I have a look?

00:07:21.470 --> 00:07:25.020
Congenital club foot.

00:07:25.020 --> 00:07:27.110
In simple language, a foot twisted inward.

00:07:27.110 --> 00:07:29.510
The cause of this twisting is not clear.

00:07:30.030 --> 00:07:36.010
Hereditary inference plays a part here, as pointed out by Dr. Little, who traces recurring deformity through four generations.

00:07:36.110 --> 00:07:37.130
Well, when you've quite finished.

00:07:40.190 --> 00:07:43.550
I say, old man, I like that.

00:07:44.690 --> 00:07:46.140
French, isn't she?

00:07:46.380 --> 00:07:47.660
Yes, she was a model in Paris.

00:07:48.140 --> 00:07:51.080
You know, I can't for the life of me understand why you gave up painting.

00:07:51.700 --> 00:07:55.610
I'd rather look at that all day long than at this.

00:07:56.420 --> 00:07:57.330
Woman, you know.

00:07:57.410 --> 00:07:59.060
You can tell by the pelvis.

00:08:00.280 --> 00:08:02.920
I like 'em with a little more...

00:08:02.920 --> 00:08:08.080
Oh, there's life in the old girl yet.

00:08:08.080 --> 00:08:09.990
Don't inhale, dearie.

00:08:09.990 --> 00:08:12.930
I say, I've got to be getting along.

00:08:12.930 --> 00:08:16.000
It's a little matter of a barmaid at the Crown on Anchor.

00:08:16.000 --> 00:08:17.960
And very nice, too.

00:08:17.960 --> 00:08:19.140
Cheerio.

00:08:19.140 --> 00:08:21.240
Funny fellow, isn't he?

00:08:21.240 --> 00:08:24.740
I say, Kerry, it must have been wonderful having that life in Paris.

00:08:24.740 --> 00:08:25.750
Well, it was.

00:08:25.750 --> 00:08:29.250
And do you mean that you really knew all those fascinating women?

00:08:29.250 --> 00:08:30.000
Well...

00:08:30.000 --> 00:08:32.360
- Some of them. - I see, you're just the man I'm looking for.

00:08:32.360 --> 00:08:34.730
- I wonder if you couldn't help me. - In what way?

00:08:34.730 --> 00:08:37.980
Well, there's a girl, and I can't get anywhere with her.

00:08:37.980 --> 00:08:40.370
And you've been to Paris and all that.

00:08:40.370 --> 00:08:42.810
I'm sure you could say something that would give me a starter.

00:08:42.810 --> 00:08:46.580
I'd ask Griffiths, only he couldn't do it and remember whom he was doing it for.

00:08:46.580 --> 00:08:48.160
Oh, but you're just the man.

00:08:48.160 --> 00:08:54.600
You know, say something to make her laugh.

00:08:54.600 --> 00:08:58.610
What? You believe it? You are too suspicious.

00:09:09.690 --> 00:09:12.200
I see. She's marvellous, isn't she?

00:09:12.200 --> 00:09:24.280
No, she's anaemic.

00:09:24.280 --> 00:09:26.720
Don't suppose she likes that bounder, do you?

00:09:26.720 --> 00:09:28.850
Of course.

00:09:28.850 --> 00:09:30.000
Now's your chance.

00:09:30.000 --> 00:09:39.630
say something. Well, I see your friend's going. I don't know what you mean. I was referring to

00:09:39.630 --> 00:09:47.610
the nobleman with a sandy moustache. Has he left you for another? Some people would do better to

00:09:47.610 --> 00:10:00.000
mind their own business. Why? You have a very nice back. Am I on speaking terms with your back? Woman, you know.

00:10:01.180 --> 00:10:03.600
You can tell by the pelvis.

00:10:03.600 --> 00:10:07.470
And that calls himself a gentleman.

00:10:07.470 --> 00:10:10.150
I apologize.

00:10:10.150 --> 00:10:11.230
What for?

00:10:11.230 --> 00:10:12.770
I promised you something charming,

00:10:12.770 --> 00:10:15.170
and she's turned out to be ill-natured and contemptible.

00:10:15.170 --> 00:10:16.450
I'm sorry I let you in for it.

00:10:16.450 --> 00:10:17.990
Oh, that's all right.

00:10:17.990 --> 00:10:20.550
You don't suppose I care what an anemic little waitress says to me, do you?

00:10:20.550 --> 00:10:23.730
Well, I do.

00:10:23.730 --> 00:10:24.780
I must be going.

00:10:24.780 --> 00:10:27.110
Coming along.

00:10:27.110 --> 00:10:28.900
I think I'll have some more tea.

00:10:56.080 --> 00:11:00.000
- Anything you want? - Yes, if you don't mind, I'd like to talk to you.

00:11:01.280 --> 00:11:03.870
Um, filthy weather, isn't it?

00:11:03.870 --> 00:11:06.310
Makes no difference to me.

00:11:06.310 --> 00:11:07.790
I have to be here all day.

00:11:07.790 --> 00:11:10.610
Oh, don't talk like that. I only wanted to say something pleasant.

00:11:10.610 --> 00:11:12.490
Well, say it.

00:11:12.490 --> 00:11:15.620
You know, you have a lovely smile.

00:11:15.620 --> 00:11:17.550
You should use it more often.

00:11:17.550 --> 00:11:19.390
Don't go spoofing me.

00:11:19.390 --> 00:11:22.610
A girl that works hard all day like I do,

00:11:22.610 --> 00:11:24.670
don't have much reason to smile.

00:11:24.670 --> 00:11:28.080
Perhaps I could find a reason.

00:11:28.080 --> 00:11:29.160
Will you let me try?

00:11:30.440 --> 00:11:33.640
Well, I don't know whether I will or whether I won't.

00:11:33.640 --> 00:11:35.220
Well, I hope you'll decide you will.

00:12:38.380 --> 00:12:48.500
Like so.

00:13:18.360 --> 00:13:19.460
with a nice little hand.

00:13:30.990 --> 00:13:35.130
- Excuse me, won't you? - Yeah, yeah.

00:13:35.130 --> 00:13:39.730
- How do you do? - You seem to be in a great hurry.

00:13:39.730 --> 00:13:46.630
- Well, I've been waiting ten minutes. - No, you could drop.

00:13:46.630 --> 00:13:49.060
- Didn't you? - That meant to be me.

00:13:49.060 --> 00:13:53.290
- Looks like you, doesn't it? - If you look at it that way.

00:13:53.290 --> 00:13:57.780
- Tea? - You are a strange sort.

00:14:00.000 --> 00:14:04.190
I say, will you dine with me some time and we'll go to the theatre?

00:14:04.190 --> 00:14:05.560
I don't mind.

00:14:05.560 --> 00:14:06.560
When will you come?

00:14:06.560 --> 00:14:08.640
I'm off Thursdays.

00:14:08.640 --> 00:14:11.020
All right, shall we say Thursday?

00:14:11.020 --> 00:14:12.020
Seven o'clock, Victoria Station.

00:14:12.020 --> 00:14:17.740
All right.

00:14:17.740 --> 00:14:20.640
I'll meet you in Victoria in the second class waiting room.

00:15:01.120 --> 00:15:03.040
Show me all tickets!

00:15:03.040 --> 00:15:05.800
All tickets, please!

00:15:05.800 --> 00:15:08.870
Show me all tickets!

00:15:08.870 --> 00:15:11.560
All tickets, please!

00:15:11.560 --> 00:15:14.220
Boat train, platform 19!

00:15:14.220 --> 00:15:20.720
All tickets, please!

00:15:20.720 --> 00:15:22.830
Well, I thought you were never coming.

00:15:22.830 --> 00:15:25.040
I like that, after keeping me waiting.

00:15:25.040 --> 00:15:27.040
I almost went home.

00:15:27.040 --> 00:15:29.540
I was in the second-class waiting room. I thought you said you'd be there.

00:15:29.540 --> 00:15:30.000
Now I say. Is it likely I'll sit in the second-class waiting room?

00:15:30.000 --> 00:15:34.700
second class when I could sit in the first? For a gentleman of brain that you don't use

00:15:34.700 --> 00:15:39.290
him, do you? Perhaps not. Anyway, you're here, so it's

00:15:39.290 --> 00:15:46.720
all right, isn't it? You certainly do make a girl feel important to you.

00:15:46.720 --> 00:15:57.080
I love that music. Whenever I hear it, I think of you.

00:15:57.080 --> 00:16:00.000
How pale you are. How strange. How cold.

00:16:05.150 --> 00:16:06.470
You are going it.

00:16:07.180 --> 00:16:08.420
Do you always order champagne?

00:16:11.010 --> 00:16:11.270
No.

00:16:11.920 --> 00:16:13.000
Then why'd you do it now?

00:16:14.720 --> 00:16:19.560
I was hoping it would make you more friendly.

00:16:22.670 --> 00:16:23.170
Do you think it will?

00:16:23.960 --> 00:16:27.130
Well, there's one thing I can say for you.

00:16:28.240 --> 00:16:30.000
Gentlemen in every sense of the word.

00:16:58.220 --> 00:16:59.190
May I see you again?

00:17:00.060 --> 00:17:09.000
mind. Doesn't it make any difference, do you? No. You don't take me out, someone else will.

00:17:33.680 --> 00:17:34.680
I'll say goodnight here.

00:17:35.550 --> 00:17:36.870
Won't you stay for a moment?

00:17:37.010 --> 00:17:37.410
No.

00:17:37.770 --> 00:17:38.210
Why not?

00:17:38.750 --> 00:17:40.950
Why? People would think I don't know what all.

00:18:41.840 --> 00:18:46.330
I love that music. Whenever I hear it, I think of you.

00:18:46.330 --> 00:18:49.240
Whenever I hear it, I think of us.

00:19:22.560 --> 00:19:29.570
- I've never danced with anyone like you. - I've been looking for you.

00:19:30.510 --> 00:19:31.130
All my life.

00:19:43.570 --> 00:19:53.040
It doesn't seem to have much to do with your time.

00:19:53.530 --> 00:19:54.710
I should be studying.

00:19:55.310 --> 00:19:56.300
And why don't you?

00:19:56.570 --> 00:19:57.750
Well, I'd rather see you.

00:19:59.500 --> 00:20:00.000
Any of the girls

00:20:00.000 --> 00:20:04.150
- Because notice you're waiting for me. - I don't know. Why, what difference does he make?

00:20:04.150 --> 00:20:07.280
- They all laugh at you, you know. - Do they? Why?

00:20:07.280 --> 00:20:16.380
- They say you're in love with me. - May I call you Mildred?

00:20:16.380 --> 00:20:21.970
- I don't mind. - Look here, don't say that anymore, will you?

00:20:21.970 --> 00:20:26.590
- Why not? - Well, alternate, I'll call you Mildred.

00:20:26.590 --> 00:20:28.640
And you call me Philip, will you?

00:20:30.060 --> 00:20:41.700
think of it. I am. I'm a little awkward at this, but will you kiss me goodnight? No. Oh, Mildred,

00:20:42.800 --> 00:20:57.260
will you come to the theatre with me on Saturday? I don't mind. You're sure they're for Saturday? Certainly.

00:21:17.690 --> 00:21:20.540
- My name is Miller, Emile Miller.

00:21:20.540 --> 00:21:21.800
We should know each other.

00:21:21.800 --> 00:21:22.820
- Why?

00:21:22.820 --> 00:21:25.980
- Well, we are both interested in the same thing.

00:21:25.980 --> 00:21:27.110
- Thing?

00:21:27.110 --> 00:21:30.000
- My dear young man, you are so, uh, so...

00:21:30.000 --> 00:21:35.090
artistic. You, you should be more...

00:21:35.090 --> 00:21:39.040
like so. Thanks. Thanks very much.

00:21:39.350 --> 00:21:49.960
That's, uh, that's all right. It changed? What time should I see you?

00:21:50.730 --> 00:21:54.610
Oh, I forgot to tell you, Philip. I can't go. Why not?

00:21:55.280 --> 00:21:55.940
Me aunt's ill.

00:22:07.960 --> 00:22:12.810
a sense in that. You don't suppose I want to go by myself, do you? I only got them for

00:22:12.810 --> 00:22:15.300
your sake. Well, you needn't go on about it.

00:22:32.240 --> 00:22:41.060
You're spying on me, and I always thought you was a gentleman at every sense of the word.

00:22:41.870 --> 00:22:42.980
Are you going out with Miller?

00:22:43.240 --> 00:22:43.620
No.

00:22:47.010 --> 00:22:48.960
Well, what if I am?

00:22:49.340 --> 00:22:51.230
I can go out with him if I want to, can't I?

00:22:51.510 --> 00:22:55.980
He's keeping you waiting, isn't he?

00:22:56.190 --> 00:22:59.070
Well, I'd rather wait for him than if you wait for me.

00:23:05.210 --> 00:23:06.130
Won't you change your mind?

00:23:06.810 --> 00:23:07.970
I'll get some more tickets and we'll...

00:23:07.970 --> 00:23:08.290
No.

00:23:14.060 --> 00:23:18.790
You keep looking for him the way I look for you.

00:23:21.850 --> 00:23:25.720
If you don't come out for me tonight, you'll never see me again.

00:23:26.330 --> 00:23:27.850
Good riddance to bad rubbish.

00:26:34.410 --> 00:26:35.610
Sorry, old boy.

00:26:35.610 --> 00:26:39.360
How about a nice large beer?

00:26:39.360 --> 00:26:41.080
Wouldn't help.

00:26:41.080 --> 00:26:42.610
Well, what would?

00:27:04.280 --> 00:27:05.850
I'll feel, leave it.

00:27:05.850 --> 00:27:07.240
Why, what for?

00:27:07.240 --> 00:27:09.350
Shows the waiter who you are.

00:27:09.350 --> 00:27:13.190
He knows who you are.

00:27:13.190 --> 00:27:18.050
So do I.

00:27:18.050 --> 00:27:19.330
What do you mean?

00:27:19.330 --> 00:27:23.200
I'm sorry, I didn't mean...

00:27:23.200 --> 00:27:26.050
You're a bit too superior for me, my fine young friend.

00:27:30.920 --> 00:27:40.260
Mildred, you don't like me. I'm crippled.

00:27:40.260 --> 00:27:41.450
Oh, Bill, isn't that?

00:27:41.450 --> 00:27:43.760
Oh, yes, I've felt it all along.

00:27:43.760 --> 00:27:45.010
Foolish.

00:27:45.010 --> 00:27:50.490
Mind my hat, silly.

00:27:50.490 --> 00:27:52.950
You are clumsy.

00:28:13.280 --> 00:28:15.040
You're off your nut. You don't know what you're doing.

00:28:15.180 --> 00:28:17.840
What sort of practice can you expect to have with a wife like that?

00:28:18.130 --> 00:28:18.770
I don't know.

00:28:19.130 --> 00:28:20.030
Let me ask you something.

00:28:20.510 --> 00:28:22.030
Why do you want to marry this girl?

00:28:23.970 --> 00:28:25.590
Because I'm so in love with her.

00:28:26.590 --> 00:28:27.110
Oh...

00:28:35.500 --> 00:28:38.480
That ring with the little design is very popular, sir.

00:28:38.480 --> 00:28:39.790
We celebrate many of them.

00:28:39.790 --> 00:28:40.810
They're 30 shillings.

00:28:40.810 --> 00:28:44.930
Thank you, sir.

00:28:44.930 --> 00:28:49.950
Philip, were you surprised by asking to take you to dinner tonight?

00:28:49.950 --> 00:28:52.140
I was delighted.

00:28:52.140 --> 00:28:52.810
Were you?

00:28:52.810 --> 00:28:53.310
Yes.

00:28:53.310 --> 00:28:54.990
Why?

00:28:54.990 --> 00:28:55.880
Oh, I don't know.

00:28:55.880 --> 00:28:57.880
You've been so sweet of me all day.

00:28:57.880 --> 00:28:59.480
I've got something to ask you.

00:29:00.000 --> 00:29:02.050
- Makes it so much easier for me.

00:29:02.050 --> 00:29:04.570
- Makes easier for me, too.

00:29:04.570 --> 00:29:05.730
I've something to tell you.

00:29:05.730 --> 00:29:10.680
- No, no, no, let me tell you first.

00:29:10.680 --> 00:29:14.490
There it is.

00:29:14.490 --> 00:29:16.460
I want you to marry me.

00:29:16.460 --> 00:29:19.050
- I'm so sorry, Philip.

00:29:19.050 --> 00:29:21.770
That's just what I was about to tell you.

00:29:21.770 --> 00:29:24.190
I shouldn't have waited so long.

00:29:24.190 --> 00:29:27.780
Fact is, I'm going to be married.

00:29:31.400 --> 00:29:34.230
Are you? To whom?

00:29:34.230 --> 00:29:38.150
A man I know. He owns very good money.

00:29:38.150 --> 00:29:41.780
Yes, I'm sure of it.

00:29:41.780 --> 00:29:47.170
Now, you won't go on about it, will you, Philip?

00:29:47.170 --> 00:29:50.680
I'm getting on for twenty-four.

00:29:50.680 --> 00:29:52.490
Time I settle down.

00:29:52.490 --> 00:29:56.020
The gentleman earns seven pounds, and Whitney's got good prospects.

00:29:56.020 --> 00:30:00.000
Well, this is goodbye. I hate to eat and run, Philip, but...

00:30:00.570 --> 00:30:02.100
Well, I have an engagement.

00:30:02.100 --> 00:30:05.060
I'm going to the theatre with the gentleman I'm going to marry.

00:31:44.810 --> 00:31:51.480
Ever since, London is the largest city in the world.

00:31:51.480 --> 00:31:53.710
And you know the cure for one woman.

00:31:53.710 --> 00:31:54.710
Another.

00:31:54.710 --> 00:31:55.700
Right-o.

00:32:06.840 --> 00:32:09.920
Nora, you don't read such junk, do you?

00:32:10.170 --> 00:32:12.120
No, I write it.

00:32:12.220 --> 00:32:12.730
What?

00:32:13.860 --> 00:32:15.270
That's how I earn my living.

00:32:15.920 --> 00:32:16.900
I didn't know.

00:32:17.410 --> 00:32:18.260
Successful?

00:32:18.360 --> 00:32:19.100
Very.

00:32:19.430 --> 00:32:22.330
I have an immense popularity amongst kitchen maids.

00:32:22.430 --> 00:32:24.830
They think me so refined.

00:32:28.560 --> 00:32:29.960
Let's not talk about that.

00:32:32.300 --> 00:32:33.260
Let's talk about us.

00:32:46.010 --> 00:32:49.960
Nora, you're not really fond of me, are you?

00:32:51.090 --> 00:32:52.600
Clever boy.

00:32:53.180 --> 00:32:55.080
You ask such foolish questions.

00:32:55.580 --> 00:32:57.790
Oh, my dear, never struck me that you could be.

00:32:58.720 --> 00:32:59.600
Pleased?

00:33:00.000 --> 00:33:05.180
and so proud and so happy and so grateful.

00:33:05.180 --> 00:33:09.080
I wish you hadn't been in love with, what was her name?

00:33:09.080 --> 00:33:11.570
Mildred.

00:33:11.570 --> 00:33:14.700
Because if she hadn't treated you so abominably,

00:33:14.700 --> 00:33:19.140
it wouldn't have taken you so long to understand how I feel.

00:33:38.190 --> 00:33:38.810
I saw you.

00:33:39.600 --> 00:33:41.120
I wasn't very quick.

00:33:42.170 --> 00:33:43.720
Let's go out and play.

00:33:46.620 --> 00:33:48.500
Until you've passed that exam.

00:34:00.830 --> 00:34:21.440
Tell me, darling, what do you get out of this?

00:34:21.440 --> 00:34:24.260
You'll never know.

00:34:24.260 --> 00:34:27.400
I'm afraid you don't get much fun with me.

00:34:27.400 --> 00:34:29.510
I wish...

00:34:31.340 --> 00:34:34.380
- If only I could take you dancing.

00:34:34.380 --> 00:34:35.690
I know how you love it.

00:34:35.690 --> 00:34:37.030
- Philip, it's very silly of you

00:34:37.030 --> 00:34:39.910
to be so sensitive about your foot.

00:34:39.910 --> 00:34:41.210
You know, other people don't think about it

00:34:41.210 --> 00:34:43.440
nearly as much as you do.

00:34:43.440 --> 00:34:44.980
They notice it when they first see you,

00:34:44.980 --> 00:34:50.740
and after that, they forget all about it.

00:34:50.740 --> 00:34:53.540
You know, I only speak of it because I love you.

00:34:53.540 --> 00:34:57.290
And I don't want it to make you unhappy.

00:34:57.290 --> 00:35:00.000
Now, will you please stay here and go on crying?

00:35:00.030 --> 00:35:15.310
There's a lady to see you, sir.

00:35:15.310 --> 00:35:16.310
Oh, is there?

00:35:16.310 --> 00:35:19.810
Yes. I shouldn't have let her in, but she was that upset, I just...

00:35:19.810 --> 00:35:20.740
Nora!

00:35:20.740 --> 00:35:29.640
What do you want?

00:35:35.310 --> 00:35:36.910
I didn't think I'd ever see you again.

00:35:36.910 --> 00:35:46.870
What's the matter?

00:35:46.870 --> 00:35:49.560
He's left me.

00:35:49.560 --> 00:35:51.510
Emo.

00:35:51.510 --> 00:35:54.940
Has he?

00:35:54.940 --> 00:35:57.810
Yes.

00:36:00.640 --> 00:36:20.650
'cause I'm going to have a baby.

00:36:20.650 --> 00:36:21.700
- Why don't you sit down?

00:36:30.960 --> 00:36:58.740
suppose you want him back. He'll never come back. Why not? He just won't, that's all. Well, you're his wife. He has to provide for you. He won't give me anything. Even if he did, I wouldn't take it. Why not? No matter what's happened, I've still got my pride. That's something, isn't it?

00:37:01.400 --> 00:37:04.420
- Have you got any money? - No.

00:37:05.250 --> 00:37:09.030
Well, you'd better get yourself a place to live.

00:37:09.710 --> 00:37:12.290
After that, we'll see what can be done.

00:37:12.630 --> 00:37:16.410
Oh, Philip, you're always so good to me.

00:37:16.520 --> 00:37:18.210
That's why I knew I could come to you.

00:37:18.210 --> 00:37:26.750
Now, look here, Mr. Miller.

00:37:26.900 --> 00:37:29.060
I'd like to know what you intend to do about Mildred.

00:37:30.000 --> 00:37:35.170
- I? What you expect me to do? - Well, I expect you to take care of her. You married her, you know.

00:37:35.170 --> 00:37:49.900
- I? I married, Mildred? - Ach, I married, uh, decent one.

00:37:49.900 --> 00:37:53.200
- Well, all the same, I'd still like to know what you intend to do about it.

00:37:53.200 --> 00:37:59.250
- Me? - I can do nothing. One man cannot solution the problem of the unmarried mother.

00:38:07.800 --> 00:38:08.680
Why didn't you tell me?

00:38:10.600 --> 00:38:12.600
I just couldn't.

00:38:14.930 --> 00:38:16.610
Well, brace up.

00:38:17.660 --> 00:38:18.500
Everything will be all right.

00:38:42.190 --> 00:38:44.860
Do you still like me?

00:38:49.560 --> 00:38:49.900
Really?

00:38:50.920 --> 00:38:53.640
Strange as it may seem, I always have.

00:38:54.320 --> 00:38:56.070
I suppose I always shall.

00:38:57.540 --> 00:38:59.840
I did everything I could to make you love me.

00:39:01.400 --> 00:39:04.310
I thought you were incapable of loving anybody.

00:39:05.480 --> 00:39:09.860
It seems horrible to think that you were willing to sacrifice everything for that man.

00:39:09.960 --> 00:39:11.240
I'm awfully sorry, Philip.

00:39:11.710 --> 00:39:15.460
You should never forget you wanted to marry me.

00:39:30.760 --> 00:39:32.860
Philip.

00:39:32.860 --> 00:39:35.570
Yes?

00:39:35.570 --> 00:39:36.570
You've been so nice to me.

00:39:36.570 --> 00:39:41.720
I'll do anything you want.

00:39:41.720 --> 00:39:44.460
Will you?

00:39:44.460 --> 00:39:45.920
Why?

00:39:45.920 --> 00:39:50.320
Why, I owe it to you.

00:39:50.320 --> 00:39:51.640
Oh, do you?

00:39:51.640 --> 00:39:57.980
You're not angry.

00:40:05.820 --> 00:40:10.060
- Then will you stay and have some dinner? - Yes, if you want me to.

00:40:10.060 --> 00:40:15.080
Of course, Philip. Nothing could you like me more.

00:40:15.080 --> 00:40:17.760
Just a moment and I'll have everything ready.

00:40:53.000 --> 00:40:53.490
- Come in.

00:41:00.190 --> 00:41:00.910
Hello, darling.

00:41:01.660 --> 00:41:05.590
Nora, how did you happen to come?

00:41:06.500 --> 00:41:08.090
Just passing by.

00:41:09.740 --> 00:41:13.150
I wanted to rub my nose against your door.

00:41:17.270 --> 00:41:20.160
Philip, why haven't I heard from you?

00:41:20.640 --> 00:41:21.750
I was just going to write.

00:41:23.080 --> 00:41:24.300
Why haven't you come to see me?

00:41:25.470 --> 00:41:26.320
Well, I...

00:41:26.320 --> 00:41:27.520
I've been busy and...

00:41:30.670 --> 00:41:31.550
Why so silent?

00:41:32.820 --> 00:41:40.070
Well, you see, Nora, I've got something strange to tell you.

00:41:41.240 --> 00:41:42.900
You've been so good to me, it only makes it harder.

00:41:46.200 --> 00:41:46.980
Philip, what's wrong?

00:41:47.740 --> 00:41:50.540
I'm sorry, it's just over.

00:41:51.780 --> 00:41:53.240
You mean you don't care for me anymore?

00:41:54.220 --> 00:41:55.650
I'm afraid so.

00:41:56.400 --> 00:41:57.610
What have I done?

00:41:58.070 --> 00:41:58.430
Nothing.

00:41:58.900 --> 00:42:00.000
You've been wonderful to me.

00:42:01.020 --> 00:42:02.120
It's just that I...

00:42:02.120 --> 00:42:10.760
Of course, I knew you never loved me as much as I love you.

00:42:11.300 --> 00:42:13.010
Yes, I'm afraid that's usually the case.

00:42:14.490 --> 00:42:18.100
There's usually one who loves and one who is loved.

00:42:18.790 --> 00:42:20.230
Oh, it's always the same.

00:42:21.340 --> 00:42:24.610
If you want a man to be nice to you, you have to be rotten to him.

00:42:25.470 --> 00:42:28.130
If you treat a man honestly, you...

00:42:33.000 --> 00:42:35.790
Philip, there's someone else.

00:42:39.590 --> 00:42:39.890
Yes.

00:42:40.680 --> 00:42:42.720
Who is she?

00:42:44.630 --> 00:42:45.030
Mildred.

00:42:45.910 --> 00:42:47.110
She's come back.

00:42:49.370 --> 00:42:53.600
After all she's done, how could you?

00:42:54.340 --> 00:42:56.470
That's what I'd like to know.

00:42:57.660 --> 00:42:59.480
Just as though you were...

00:43:00.090 --> 00:43:01.450
Found her in some way.

00:43:02.810 --> 00:43:03.270
Yes.

00:43:04.530 --> 00:43:05.610
As I am to you.

00:43:07.290 --> 00:43:08.700
As she was to Miller.

00:43:10.260 --> 00:43:11.690
As every human being is.

00:43:12.380 --> 00:43:13.700
To something or other.

00:43:22.630 --> 00:43:29.770
A looking little thing, isn't it?

00:43:30.760 --> 00:43:32.770
I can't believe it's mine.

00:43:32.770 --> 00:43:43.220
- No, if you'll excuse me.

00:43:43.220 --> 00:43:45.930
- So glad it's over, darling.

00:43:45.930 --> 00:43:48.410
- You've been so good to me, Philip.

00:43:48.410 --> 00:43:57.340
Now on, things will be different.

00:43:57.340 --> 00:44:00.000
- Now you will take good care of her, won't you?

00:44:00.000 --> 00:44:01.160
But I will, Mum.

00:44:01.160 --> 00:44:06.050
- Good day. - Good day.

00:44:06.050 --> 00:44:12.840
I know you don't like it, Philip.

00:44:12.840 --> 00:44:15.490
I can't do anything else if I'm going to work.

00:44:15.490 --> 00:44:16.930
No, I suppose not.

00:44:16.930 --> 00:44:20.400
But be sure and go over on Sundays

00:44:20.400 --> 00:44:22.310
and see the baby's properly taken care of.

00:44:22.310 --> 00:44:24.250
I will.

00:44:24.250 --> 00:44:28.360
What are we going to do this afternoon?

00:44:30.000 --> 00:44:31.480
Uh, I asked Griffiths to come over.

00:44:32.290 --> 00:44:33.290
Oh, did you?

00:44:34.820 --> 00:44:35.260
Why?

00:44:35.850 --> 00:44:41.040
Well, I know you find him amusing, and I'm always afraid of boring you.

00:44:49.080 --> 00:44:49.980
Hello, hello, hello!

00:44:50.700 --> 00:44:51.570
Sorry I'm late.

00:44:53.080 --> 00:44:54.220
Had to get rid of a girl.

00:44:54.550 --> 00:44:55.680
Why didn't you bring her along?

00:44:55.980 --> 00:44:57.760
Oh, I'm not interested in my girl.

00:44:58.140 --> 00:45:00.000
I'm only interested in other men's girls.

00:45:01.470 --> 00:45:06.190
Do you like me?

00:45:06.190 --> 00:45:13.530
Really, I'm too hungry to know, but I think I like you lots.

00:45:13.530 --> 00:45:16.640
I'd like you a lot more if you got him to take us out to dinner tonight.

00:45:16.640 --> 00:45:18.320
And if you do, I'll tell you some funny stories.

00:45:18.320 --> 00:45:20.480
And you'll laugh and think you're having a wonderful time.

00:45:20.480 --> 00:45:22.440
What will he do?

00:45:22.440 --> 00:45:26.760
Oh, pay the bill.

00:45:31.850 --> 00:45:42.680
"Bill, your missus? I'm sorry, I thought it was your sister!"

00:46:08.480 --> 00:46:13.270
- Good night, Philip.

00:46:13.270 --> 00:46:19.550
- Good night.

00:46:19.550 --> 00:46:26.850
- Wait a moment.

00:46:26.850 --> 00:46:27.850
Are you in love with Mildred?

00:46:27.850 --> 00:46:29.410
- I?

00:46:30.190 --> 00:46:34.290
So that's what you've been so funny about, huh?

00:46:34.650 --> 00:46:36.150
Well, my dear old boy, I...

00:46:36.150 --> 00:46:37.500
It doesn't matter to you, Harry.

00:46:37.560 --> 00:46:38.440
You've got so many women.

00:46:40.620 --> 00:46:41.860
Don't take Mildred away from me.

00:46:43.030 --> 00:46:45.850
But my dear old boy, she's nothing to me at all.

00:46:46.490 --> 00:46:47.950
Nothing at all.

00:47:04.510 --> 00:47:05.510
Do you like it, Philip?

00:47:05.510 --> 00:47:06.850
Very much.

00:47:06.850 --> 00:47:09.920
So nice of you to give it to me.

00:47:09.920 --> 00:47:18.430
What are you thinking about?

00:47:18.430 --> 00:47:21.890
You were having quite a flirtation with Griffiths last night.

00:47:21.890 --> 00:47:24.320
Yes, I was, wasn't I?

00:47:24.320 --> 00:47:29.220
As a matter of fact, well, I'm sort of in love with him.

00:47:30.440 --> 00:47:31.860
Ah, I'm not surprised.

00:47:31.860 --> 00:47:33.330
Why, what do you mean?

00:47:33.330 --> 00:47:36.870
Well, Griffiths is good-looking, he's amusing, he says the kind of things that make you laugh.

00:47:36.870 --> 00:47:40.310
Ah, thank you not to make fun of me. You're a bit too superior for me, my fine young friend.

00:47:40.310 --> 00:47:42.070
Oh, good heavens, Mildred, I wasn't making fun of you.

00:47:42.070 --> 00:47:43.670
Well, you certainly don't act as if it's serious.

00:47:43.670 --> 00:47:44.470
Well, I don't think it is.

00:47:44.470 --> 00:47:45.590
Oh, you don't, eh? Why not?

00:47:45.590 --> 00:47:46.870
Because Griffiths isn't in love with you.

00:47:46.870 --> 00:47:48.130
How do you know?

00:47:48.130 --> 00:47:49.080
I asked him.

00:47:49.080 --> 00:47:54.900
Would you like to read a letter I got from him this morning?

00:48:01.920 --> 00:48:03.740
I've been up all night thinking about you,

00:48:04.560 --> 00:48:07.000
and I've just sent for a special messenger

00:48:07.000 --> 00:48:08.620
who will take this to you in the dawn.

00:48:10.730 --> 00:48:14.530
You've no notion of the time I had with your friend last night.

00:48:15.620 --> 00:48:17.930
He kept asking me if I love you,

00:48:17.970 --> 00:48:19.310
and of course, what could I say?

00:48:21.220 --> 00:48:22.500
He'll doubtless tell you all this,

00:48:22.580 --> 00:48:24.900
so I'm making sure that you...

00:48:32.940 --> 00:48:36.470
Well, hell, but if I love him, can I?

00:48:36.740 --> 00:48:38.070
No, I suppose not, but...

00:48:38.070 --> 00:48:39.190
Then what's going on about?

00:48:39.680 --> 00:48:40.110
Nothing.

00:48:41.460 --> 00:48:43.940
Only I was fool enough to think that you cared for me.

00:48:44.350 --> 00:48:45.290
You do, Philip.

00:48:45.970 --> 00:48:46.750
He's a friend.

00:48:48.530 --> 00:48:49.650
Not in any other way.

00:48:51.400 --> 00:48:54.080
But you do care for Griffiths in the other way.

00:48:56.850 --> 00:48:58.430
But you're rather cold.

00:48:58.590 --> 00:49:00.000
That sort of thing doesn't mean anything.

00:49:00.000 --> 00:49:15.750
to you? That's what you think. There's no use going on about it, Philip.

00:49:17.120 --> 00:49:29.510
Said yourself I couldn't help it if I'm in love with him. Anything else to be said, say it.

00:49:32.200 --> 00:49:35.280
That's a nice dress you have on, Mildred.

00:49:35.280 --> 00:49:38.060
I couldn't afford it, but I paid for it.

00:49:38.060 --> 00:49:40.890
You have a nice apartment.

00:49:40.890 --> 00:49:42.400
I couldn't afford it, but I paid for it.

00:49:42.400 --> 00:49:43.700
If you're a gentleman,

00:49:43.700 --> 00:49:45.800
do you think you'd throw what you've done for me in the face?

00:49:45.800 --> 00:49:48.680
Do you think it matters to me whether I'm a gentleman or not?

00:49:48.680 --> 00:49:49.580
If I were a gentleman,

00:49:49.580 --> 00:49:52.410
you don't suppose I'd care for a cheap bugger little?

00:49:52.410 --> 00:49:55.600
I'm sorry, Philip.

00:49:55.600 --> 00:49:57.960
I didn't want to end this way.

00:50:02.520 --> 00:50:04.300
- Harry's waiting for me.

00:50:04.300 --> 00:50:06.910
- What do you intend to do?

00:50:06.910 --> 00:50:10.380
- We're going to Paris.

00:50:10.380 --> 00:50:12.440
- Get out, get out.

00:51:03.610 --> 00:51:10.380
I've moved three times and each time this woman's hounded me down I don't like

00:51:10.380 --> 00:51:21.640
to do this but all right sir I'll move on come on can't stay here come on now

00:51:44.360 --> 00:51:46.290
Look here, Carrie. Mildred and I are all washed up.

00:51:46.290 --> 00:51:47.250
That's too bad.

00:51:47.250 --> 00:51:51.090
If you'll excuse me, I'm due in the ward.

00:52:09.880 --> 00:52:13.000
- Anything interesting, Carrie?

00:52:13.000 --> 00:52:15.280
I was just thinking what an unusual name you have.

00:52:15.280 --> 00:52:16.750
- It's a very old Yorkshire name.

00:52:16.750 --> 00:52:19.480
Once took a day's riding across our estates.

00:52:19.480 --> 00:52:21.820
And here I am in a charity hospital

00:52:21.820 --> 00:52:25.890
because my father loved fast women and slow horses.

00:52:25.890 --> 00:52:27.620
How the mighty are fallen.

00:52:32.300 --> 00:52:36.030
Hello, father.

00:52:36.030 --> 00:52:44.380
Carrie, this is my daughter, christened Maria Del Sol, her mother always called her Sally.

00:52:44.380 --> 00:52:48.770
This young man is a student here, he's been very nice to me, and with some inducement,

00:52:48.770 --> 00:52:50.270
he might be nice to you.

00:52:50.270 --> 00:52:56.910
Now, father, father's particular genius is saying the wrong thing, he thinks it's fun

00:52:56.910 --> 00:52:57.910
to embarrass me.

00:52:57.910 --> 00:52:58.910
It is!

00:52:58.910 --> 00:53:00.000
Why don't you do that?

00:53:00.000 --> 00:53:04.900
try it sometime, Carrie. I will if I get the chance. You shall have it. You're coming to

00:53:04.900 --> 00:53:09.540
see us the first Sunday I'm home. Oh yes, please do.

00:53:36.110 --> 00:53:41.270
Yes, it is, but it's not very sanitary.

00:53:41.270 --> 00:53:43.270
Tanitation be hanged. Give me art.

00:53:43.270 --> 00:53:46.190
I've got nine children and they thrive on bad dreams.

00:53:46.190 --> 00:53:48.070
Look at that now.

00:53:48.070 --> 00:53:50.950
I am with great admiration.

00:53:50.950 --> 00:53:56.390
Shall I bring the ale, Father?

00:53:56.390 --> 00:53:58.040
Right, my girl. The sooner the better.

00:54:00.510 --> 00:54:02.570
I hope you didn't have the table in here on my account.

00:54:03.290 --> 00:54:06.090
I'd have been quite happy to have had dinner with Mrs. Athelny and the children.

00:54:06.250 --> 00:54:06.850
Oh, no.

00:54:07.150 --> 00:54:08.840
I always take meals by myself.

00:54:09.120 --> 00:54:10.520
I like these antique customs.

00:54:11.700 --> 00:54:14.280
I don't think women ought to sit down at table with men.

00:54:14.480 --> 00:54:15.120
Oh, don't you?

00:54:15.320 --> 00:54:15.820
Why not?

00:54:16.040 --> 00:54:17.240
It ruins conversation.

00:54:19.830 --> 00:54:20.960
I'm sure it's very bad for them.

00:54:21.190 --> 00:54:22.510
It puts ideas in their heads.

00:54:22.930 --> 00:54:25.890
And women are never at ease with themselves when they have ideas.

00:54:26.620 --> 00:54:28.120
You sound like the voice of old England.

00:54:28.420 --> 00:54:29.240
I am, sir.

00:54:29.240 --> 00:54:30.000
And it's...

00:54:30.000 --> 00:54:33.240
It's this fine old Yorkshire pudding that gives me strength to carry on.

00:54:34.600 --> 00:54:38.100
Now stop getting up and down like a jumping jack every time she comes into the room.

00:54:38.300 --> 00:54:40.660
She doesn't want you to make a fuss about her, do you, Sally?

00:54:40.920 --> 00:54:44.240
And she won't get rude if you sit still while she waits on you.

00:54:44.890 --> 00:54:47.690
She don't care to hang for chivalry, do you, Sally?

00:54:48.380 --> 00:54:49.360
No, Father.

00:54:49.730 --> 00:54:52.930
You speak quietly while I eat the young man so boldly.

00:54:53.480 --> 00:54:56.280
Yes, Father.

00:54:57.780 --> 00:54:59.570
You know what I'm talking about, Sally?

00:55:00.120 --> 00:55:02.310
How could I, darling? You're so clever.

00:55:03.350 --> 00:55:05.790
Don't say I might cheer in order to make eyes at him.

00:55:07.150 --> 00:55:09.130
Better get Philip some more ale.

00:55:15.280 --> 00:55:23.110
Is there anything better than English ale?

00:55:23.850 --> 00:55:29.170
Let us thank God for simple pleasures, a good appetite, roast beef and beer.

00:55:31.120 --> 00:55:32.820
I was married to a lady once.

00:55:37.080 --> 00:55:38.230
Never marry a lady, my lord.

00:55:38.880 --> 00:55:39.660
Oh, really? Why?

00:55:40.060 --> 00:55:44.600
Because a lady has a point of view, a personality, and an individuality.

